[00:02.135] I remember the time we met by the shore
[00:07.322] I found you holding what I cannot say enough
[00:13.000] The tragedy on your back flowed in
[00:15.784] The swaying little stars on the waltz
[00:18.809] A blink of life your eyes caught in that night
[00:27.608] Hoping that no end rends us to be with you
[00:32.893] Embed a wish into the woven white flowers
[00:38.818] The loving and full bright voice that You
[00:41.855] gave me no matter when you called my name
[00:44.516] Even as time goes by I can let it play now Refuses to fade out
[00:50.030] With the daisy crown
[00:52.104] The moonlight palely poured down
[00:54.986] The humming of slumber
[00:57.776] A dream's tear made your cheek wet
[01:01.713] Embracing soft and glowing warmth
[01:04.508] Let me lie down beside you giving all my heart
[01:07.594] Now I know by sharing our warmth
[01:10.381] We came closer
[01:24.804] I made myself fade into the deeper shadows
[01:30.211] I listened to the ringing as you prayed more
[01:35.917] That was the only thing I could do
[01:38.792] I kept a silent secret just for you here
[01:41.848] What matters in the end is not the shape
[01:44.210] But you you hold it tight
[01:57.041] Purely satisfied only to play with toys together
[02:02.546] Maybe I'm shaped by thousands of memories of you
[02:08.159] Together we hold the old dusty film
[02:11.138] Even though it no longer goes the way it used to
[02:13.337] Reach for a rest remember I'm here for you
[02:25.176] With the daisy crown
[02:27.354] The moonlight palely poured down
[02:30.131] The humming of slumber
[02:33.013] A girl bathed in the pale light
[02:36.841] Embracing soft and glowing warmth
[02:39.947] Do you remember me on the dark and lone night?
[02:42.843] It lets you know we're sharing our warmth however far
[02:50.814] On the daisy crown
[02:52.837] I had a dream so warm
[02:55.758] Than the midday sun and glow
[02:58.694] A dream stays with me warmer
[03:02.317] To the memory that might fade if I blink once again
[03:05.282] I let myself lie down
[03:06.879] In dreams I'm with you
